From c438f5c0b0669b871c8e4428ea36b3b6526426d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:39:09 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] feat(desktop): Stations tab shows training stations as
 in-sample
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the bundled summary carries byStationTrain (1.3.0 current line), the
Stations tab gets a held-out / training / all switch that defaults to
held-out, so the first view is unchanged. Every row carries a HELD-OUT or
TRAIN · IN-SAMPLE badge, an amber banner explains that training-station
scores are optimistic whenever they are shown, and the KPI tiles count
held-out stations only with a note naming what is excluded. The station
dialog shows the split and swaps the held-out note for an in-sample one.
Summaries without training rows render exactly as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
